{
"dur": 50.895,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 10.038,
"text": "Then, far away in Syria, everything changed. In 750 a rival family, the Abbasids, overthrew the Umayyads and hunted down almost every member of the royal family.",
"end": 10.313
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 10.313,
"vo_start": 10.588,
"vo_end": 19.188,
"text": "One young prince escaped. Abd al-Rahman, about twenty years old, ran with his little brother and jumped into the Euphrates river with soldiers behind them.",
"end": 19.463
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 19.463,
"vo_start": 19.738,
"vo_end": 27.096,
"text": "The soldiers promised safety if they came back. His brother turned around and was killed. Abd al-Rahman kept swimming.",
"end": 27.371
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 27.371,
"vo_start": 27.646,
"vo_end": 32.486,
"text": "He spent about five years on the run across North Africa, hiding with his mother's Berber relatives.",
"end": 32.761
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 32.761,
"vo_start": 33.036,
"vo_end": 42.07,
"text": "In 755 he landed in Al-Andalus. Within a year he took Cordoba and declared himself emir. Al-Andalus now answered to nobody in the east.",
"end": 42.345
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 42.345,
"vo_start": 42.62,
"vo_end": 49.945,
"text": "He started building the Great Mosque of Cordoba on the site of an old church. Its forest of red and white striped arches is still standing.",
"end": 50.895
}
],
